Fly By

BLUF: Flight tracker application

Running the App (First Time):
1. Clone this repo
    git clone <url-of-this-repo>.git

2. Navigate to the root of the repo in your terminal
    cd <path-to-this-repo>/app

3. Build image for container(s)
    docker build --tag ashtonrwsmith/fly-by .

4. List images and ensure it's there
    docker images -a

5. Run the container detached (background) and publish port 8008 to the host machine
    docker run --detach --name fly-by --publish 8008:8008 ashtonrwsmith/fly-by

6. Ensure container is up
    docker ps -a

7. Navigate to the app in browser
    http://localhost:8008


Useful Commands:
docker stop fly-by
docker start fly-by
    - Self explanitory
open -a Docker
    - Get Docker up and running (daemon)


Refreshing App:
Included in this repo is a shell script to rebuild the image, delete any existing containers, and restarting a container with new image

chmod +x refresh.sh
    - On first time, run this to make it executable
./refresh.sh
    - Runs the script (use ../<name> if in /app dir)


Useful Docs:
https://openskynetwork.github.io/opensky-api/python.html#opensky_api.OpenSkyStates
    - OpenSky Python API which gives us flight data

https://leafletjs.com/
    - Leaflet JS which gives us our map/tile